1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,080
Hello English learners, welcome back to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:05,600
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:06,820
And I'm Erica.

4
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:14,520
And today we're bringing you part 9 of our romantic drama suspense action series, I'm Sorry I Love You.

5
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,280
This is actually our penultimate lesson.

6
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:21,900
Exactly, this story will end in part 10, so we're almost done.

7
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:22,540
What's happening?

8
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:30,240
Well, I am pretty excited to find out, so why don't we go straight into the dialogue and catch up with Steven and Veronica.

9
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:38,090
Veronica, wait.

10
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:39,690
Come on, honey, get back in the car.

11
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:40,870
Let's talk it over, okay?

12
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,390
No, I'm tired of your lies.

13
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,610
I don't know who you are anymore.

14
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:49,930
Veronica, it's me, the man that has and always will love you.

15
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:52,510
I'm sorry that I've lied to you, believe me.

16
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:54,230
It's been hard for me as well.

17
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,980
And time and again, I've thought of coming clean.

18
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:58,850
But I couldn't put you or my mission at risk.

19
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:00,270
It's all over now.

20
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:01,290
My assignment is complete.

21
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,070
And now I have to go back to India.

22
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:04,210
What?

23
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:05,210
Are you kidding?

24
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:08,710
Is there anything else I should know before I never see you again?

25
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:11,010
How could you deceive me like that?

26
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:12,010
Yes.

27
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:22,100
Veronica, I know that this isn't the best time and you probably hate me right now, but I want to be completely forthright with you.

28
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:26,440
I know deep in my heart that you are the best thing that has ever happened to me.

29
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,470
Veronica, will you marry me?

30
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:31,540
Come with me to India, baby.

31
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:36,060
I can't make it for everything that's happened, but I can promise you my undying love.

32
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:40,360
I will be the most devoted husband and I will cherish you always.

33
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:45,840
Steven, I can't just leave everything at the drop of a hat.

34
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:49,780
With everything that has happened between us, I just don't know you anymore.

35
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:53,900
I just can't build a relationship on a foundation of lies.

36
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,720
I do love you, but I can't go with you.

37
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:58,920
I'm sorry.

38
00:01:59,360 --> 00:01:59,960
I love you.

39
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:13,830
This is the last call for flight A15 from Los Angeles to Hyderabad.

40
00:02:15,310 --> 00:02:16,610
I'm sorry, sir.

41
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:17,790
We can't wait any longer.

42
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:19,450
You must board the plane.

43
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:21,250
Are you waiting for someone?

44
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:25,190
I was, but I don't think she's coming.

45
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,940
All right, so it seems like our poor Steven is going home by himself.

46
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:44,600
It's so sad.

47
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:45,280
I know.

48
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:50,640
he proposed, she didn't accept, and now he's going back to India by himself.

49
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:59,450
I think this must be one of the worst feelings in the world, wondering if the person you love is going to show up at the last minute and realizing they aren't.

50
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:09,790
I think it's very common of movies, you always expect the person to come running and show up, but as you can see, our dialogues are more realistic, so it didn't happen in this occasion.

51
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,600
More realistic.

52
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:12,600
Okay.

53
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,640
Anyway, let's not debate that topic.

54
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:17,800
Let's go straight into the language now with Language Takeaway.

55
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:20,810
Language Takeaway.

56
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:29,480
All right, so today on Language Takeaway, we have six words that we're going to be looking at and let's get started with the first one.

57
00:03:29,490 --> 00:03:33,350
Okay, so we've got language about love and language about telling the truth.

58
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:36,970
And the first one is a word about telling the truth.

59
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:41,440
So Steven said, I've thought of coming clean.

60
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,810
Okay, to come clean.

61
00:03:43,130 --> 00:03:43,730
To come clean.

62
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:47,910
Now if I want to come clean, it means I want to...

63
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:52,490
You want to admit to something or to tell the truth about something you've been hiding.

64
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:53,210
Exactly.

65
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:56,930
Okay, so I want to finally tell the truth or confess.

66
00:03:57,450 --> 00:04:01,550
So someone needs to come clean about who stole the chocolate out of the kitchen.

67
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:03,070
Okay, come clean.

68
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:09,510
So Steven wanted to come clean on many occasions, but Veronica said, how could you deceive me like that?

69
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:11,440
Deceive someone.

70
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,860
How could you deceive me?

71
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,420
So to deceive someone.

72
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:19,040
All right, to deceive.

73
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:24,180
When you deceive somebody, you make them believe something that is untrue.

74
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:26,360
So you kind of trick them.

75
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:27,100
Yeah, yeah.

76
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:31,480
Okay, make them believe or see something that is not really true.

77
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:32,840
Exactly.

78
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:35,330
All right, so that's the verb, to deceive.

79
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:40,160
Now the noun, the action of doing this is called deception.

80
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,690
It was all a great deception.

81
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:45,530
Okay, so a big trick, something, a big untruth.

82
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:46,810
You deceived me.

83
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:48,810
All right, very good.

84
00:04:48,990 --> 00:04:51,430
And now the opposite of deceive.

85
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:53,690
Is to be forthright.

86
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:55,520
Forthright.

87
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,850
So Steven wants to be completely forthright with Veronica.

88
00:04:59,430 --> 00:05:01,750
Okay, I want to be forthright with you.

89
00:05:02,230 --> 00:05:07,110
All right, when you are forthright with somebody, you are very honest and truthful with them, right?

90
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:07,390
Direct.

91
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,800
You don't defend everything directly.

92
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,070
So you don't hide it or soften it or anything.

93
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:14,960
Very good.

94
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:15,530
So forthright.

95
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:20,090
All right, so three words about honesty.

96
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,700
Now we've got three words about love for you.

97
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:26,160
So Steven promised Veronica his undying love.

98
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,360
My undying love.

99
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,480
My undying love.

100
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:31,180
Now undying.

101
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:33,520
Well, I think it's pretty easy, right?

102
00:05:33,780 --> 00:05:34,420
It won't die.

103
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,660
It won't die, exactly.

104
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:39,020
So he's offering her his love forever.

105
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:41,840
A very romantic phrase.

106
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,240
Very romantic.

107
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:45,250
And he also promised to be a devoted husband.

108
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:46,830
Devoted husband.

109
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,910
I'll be the most devoted husband.

110
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,810
Now this word devoted, what am I saying there?

111
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:57,690
So as a devoted husband, Steven really, really would love his wife.

112
00:05:58,040 --> 00:06:03,110
He'd really look after her well and he would put all of his energy into his marriage, right?

113
00:06:03,290 --> 00:06:05,830
Okay, so he would be very committed to her.

114
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:07,590
And work really hard.

115
00:06:08,090 --> 00:06:11,550
Now can I change the noun husband for something else?

116
00:06:11,770 --> 00:06:14,150
Yeah, we can talk about a devoted friend.

117
00:06:14,610 --> 00:06:15,790
Or a devoted father.

118
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,530
Or a devoted employee.

119
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:18,630
Very good.

120
00:06:19,090 --> 00:06:21,010
And our last word about love.

121
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:25,400
Well, Steven also promises to cherish Veronica.

122
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:28,320
Okay, I will cherish you always.

123
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,940
I will cherish you always.

124
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:33,100
So if I cherish somebody like my girlfriend, what would that mean?

125
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:39,910
That means you hold her in your heart, like you really love her and you really respect her and you hold her close in your heart.

126
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:44,370
Okay, so I respect her and maybe you don't take that person for granted.

127
00:06:45,670 --> 00:06:46,630
To cherish someone.

128
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,080
Yeah.

129
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:55,310
Alright, so some nice honesty words, some nice love words and I think now we can move on to some interesting phrases with Fluency Builder.

130
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:57,600
Fluency Builder.

131
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,300
Alright, so Veronica was upset.

132
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:06,080
She didn't want to get back in the car and Steven said, let's talk it over, okay?

133
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,200
Let's talk it over.

134
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,740
Let's talk it over.

135
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,440
To talk something over.

136
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:15,440
Now if I tell you that I want to talk it over, what am I saying?

137
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:17,440
Well obviously you want to talk about it, right?

138
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:21,160
But you want to talk about it for some time.

139
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:24,880
To really talk about all of the problems and the issues and everything.

140
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:27,140
So to try and make things clear.

141
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:27,930
Exactly.

142
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,680
Alright.

143
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:34,720
So when he was confessing, he said, time and again I've thought of coming clean.

144
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,550
So this phrase, time and again.

145
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,170
Time and again.

146
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,030
Time and again.

147
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:42,730
So that's basically the same as saying again and again or many times.

148
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:44,120
Right.

149
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:48,250
So time and again I've thought of quitting smoking but never really have done it.

150
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:51,050
So you've thought many times of doing it.

151
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,190
Time and again.

152
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:53,720
Yep.

153
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,750
Alright, so let's go to our next phrase.

154
00:07:56,160 --> 00:08:01,440
Now Veronica said, I can't just leave everything at the drop of a hat.

155
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,570
At the drop of a hat.

156
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,130
At the drop of a hat.

157
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:08,650
So this is a very interesting and colloquial way of saying immediately.

158
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,450
So why don't we hear a few examples of how this is used in English.

159
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:16,290
Example one.

160
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,390
My boss expects me to come into work at the drop of a hat.

161
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:22,340
Example two.

162
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,570
Laura is always willing to help me at the drop of a hat.

163
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:28,860
Example three.

164
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:31,900
I can't leave at the drop of a hat.

165
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,100
I need time to prepare.

166
00:08:34,290 --> 00:08:40,010
Okay, so as you can see, you can change it for different things but basically you're saying I can't do something immediately.

167
00:08:40,710 --> 00:08:45,790
Yeah, and it is almost always attached to this idea of doing something or going somewhere, being somewhere.

168
00:08:46,450 --> 00:08:47,270
Very good.

169
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,310
At the drop of a hat.

170
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:51,770
Alright, now our final phrase here for this lesson.

171
00:08:52,290 --> 00:09:00,810
So Veronica was saying I can't go to India at the drop of a hat and she also said I just can't build a relationship on a foundation of lies.

172
00:09:01,450 --> 00:09:03,510
Okay, a foundation of lies.

173
00:09:03,850 --> 00:09:05,870
To build something on a foundation of lies.

174
00:09:06,390 --> 00:09:07,290
Now this is interesting.

175
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:08,490
Let's take a look at this.

176
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:11,280
Foundation what is that?

177
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,330
Well you know you have a house, right?

178
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:17,170
And the part that's in the ground that supports the house is the foundation.

179
00:09:17,450 --> 00:09:19,830
Okay, so it supports the entire structure.

180
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:21,440
Right.

181
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:25,680
So here she refers to the lies as the foundation.

182
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:29,200
And that's no way to start a strong relationship, is it?

183
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,200
Exactly.

184
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:37,380
So we use it metaphorically in this way but we can always, but we always have to say it, but we always have to use the verb build.

185
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:41,920
Okay, so it's basically to make something on a base of something else, right?

186
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:48,760
So for example, a strong relationship is built on a foundation of trust.

187
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:52,540
Or this country was built on a foundation of liberty.

188
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:53,700
Very good.

189
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:57,360
So always use foundation with built.

190
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:57,530
Very good.

191
00:09:58,360 --> 00:09:59,360
Very interesting.

192
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:06,120
And well I think we should listen to this dialogue for the last time and then we'll come back and talk a little bit more about Veronica and Steven.

193
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:13,720
Veronica, wait.

194
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:14,600
Come on, honey.

195
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:15,320
Get back in the car.

196
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:16,460
Let's talk it over, okay?

197
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,320
No.

198
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,020
I'm tired of your lies.

199
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,160
I don't know who you are anymore.

200
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:25,550
Veronica, it's me, the man that has and always will love you.

201
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,140
I'm sorry that I've lied to you, believe me.

202
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:31,800
It's been hard for me as well and time and again I've thought of coming clean.

203
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,500
But I couldn't put you or my mission at risk.

204
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:35,900
It's all over now.

205
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:38,740
My assignment is complete and now I have to go back to India.

206
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:39,820
What?

207
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:40,860
Are you kidding?

208
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:44,340
Is there anything else I should know before I never see you again?

209
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:46,640
How could you deceive me like that?

210
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:47,660
Yes.

211
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:57,720
Veronica, I know that this isn't the best time and you probably hate me right now but I want to be completely forthright with you.

212
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:02,080
I know deep in my heart that you are the best thing that has ever happened to me.

213
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:05,120
Veronica, will you marry me?

214
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,170
Come with me to India, baby.

215
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:11,690
I can't make it for everything that's happened but I can promise you my undying love.

216
00:11:12,390 --> 00:11:15,990
I will be the most devoted husband and I will cherish you always.

217
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:22,200
Stephen, I can't just leave everything at the drop of a hat.

218
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:25,400
With everything that has happened between us, I just don't know you anymore.

219
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:29,540
I just can't build a relationship on a foundation of lies.

220
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,340
I do love you but I can't go with you.

221
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:34,500
I'm sorry.

222
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:35,600
I love you.

223
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:49,440
This is the last call for flight A15 from Los Angeles to Hyderabad.

224
00:11:51,010 --> 00:11:52,250
I'm sorry, sir.

225
00:11:52,410 --> 00:11:53,410
We can't wait any longer.

226
00:11:53,690 --> 00:11:55,090
You must board the plane.

227
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:56,870
Are you waiting for someone?

228
00:11:57,670 --> 00:12:00,790
I was but I don't think she's coming.

229
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:17,600
So Marco, I think I see a bit of a tear there in the corner of your eye.

230
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:18,680
I'm very sad.

231
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,960
I can't believe he proposed and she just said no.

232
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:22,280
Just like that.

233
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:24,280
Well, it's not supposed to happen.

234
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:29,160
Plus, he was inviting her to India and exotic getaway and promising.

235
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:32,460
Exotic getaway for the rest of her life.

236
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,260
Well, what do you think will happen?

237
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,280
Part 10, it all ends.

238
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:41,680
So do you think they all just keep on living their separate lives?

239
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,280
Will they meet again?

240
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:43,720
Who knows?

241
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:46,700
Come to our website and tell us what you think will happen.

242
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,120
So you can find us at EnglishPod.com.

243
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,300
All right.

244
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:55,080
Don't miss our finale of this lesson and until next time, we'll see you guys there.
